  "origin": "baseline",
  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 8, P = 12. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[10, 3, 11, 0, 4, 3, 11, 9], [4, 4, 11, 9, 11, 8, 1, 1], [8, 0, 4, 6, 11, 3, 7, 0]], sigma = [3, 6, 5, 0, 7, 2, 1, 4], B = [2, 5, 9, 2, 6, 9, 5, 6].",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data"
  ],
  "date": "2026",
  "novelty": "known_parameters",
  "notes": "Literature baseline: a reproduction of a code published with arXiv:2609.30069, rebuilt from the authors' data repository (https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data/blob/306b31d/codes/reverse_fold/j3l8/specs/reverse_j3l8_p12_k14.json). Not a new construction. The authors report d = 6 as exact. Their lower-bound search output is not in the repository, so this entry carries an upper bound backed by their weight-6 Pauli logical, stored as the witness."
